 "not_run": {
  "two_level_touch+gff": "not runnable on the real arm in either form. Behind recover_first (the MuJoCo row) the blind recovery's re-hold after its first J2 seek ran away on the real arm at 91-93 deg/s powered, every start (run real_two_level_touch_gff_*, the plant's controlled stop and the home button each time). Bare (the home button as the recovery), its first seek carries the gravity feed-forward planned for the upper stop (J2 6.6 N.m) from the hanging rest, where gravity is ~0: on the MuJoCo rung that lunges J2 to 3.4 rad/s and the sequence's own speed guard aborts it (B0 and B2, home start) - not sent to the arm.",
  "press_reverse+gff": "not run on the real arm: its second side walks J2 to -85 deg (Craig 5) and seeks J2's lower stop (CAD -90.03 = Craig ~0), below the unidentified contact the real arm meets at Craig j2 12.6 / 16.5 deg (fivebar-real-night F08, two stalls on one map; fivebar_homed.LADDER_J2_MIN_DEG 20 keeps every stage above it). It would press up to 10 N.m into that contact and define it as J2's lower stop: a guaranteed wrong zero and an unknown thing pressed. Needs the contact identified (Zach's eye at j2 ~17) or a second side that stays above j2 20."
 },
